          "**Prime a new pMDI** (or one unused for over a week) by spraying 1-2 puffs into the air, and **count doses** if there is no counter - floating the canister in water is unreliable. [GINA 2025]",
          "**pMDI with spacer (adults and children over 5)**: (1) shake and fit inhaler to spacer; (2) breathe out; (3) seal lips on spacer mouthpiece; (4) **one puff into the spacer**; (5) either one slow deep breath held 10 seconds, or **4-5 normal breaths**; (6) repeat for each puff, one at a time - the spacer removes the need for coordination and **halves throat deposition**. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Spacer in young children**: **0-3 years use a spacer with a tight-fitting face mask; 4-5 years use a spacer with mouthpiece**; one puff at a time with **5-10 tidal breaths per puff**; a crying child inhales very little, so give it when calm or asleep. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Spacer care**: wash monthly in warm water with washing-up liquid, **do not rinse or wipe - let it air-dry** so a film reduces static; in an emergency a **500 mL plastic bottle with the inhaler sealed into its base** works as a spacer. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Rotacap (single-dose capsule DPI)**: (1) with dry hands take the capsule out of the strip just before use and place it in the chamber; (2) close or twist to pierce it; (3) **breathe out away from the device**; (4) seal lips and **breathe in fast and deep** (the capsule should rattle); (5) hold the breath 5-10 seconds; (6) **open and check the capsule is empty** - inhale again if powder remains; (7) discard the capsule. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Rotacap errors specific to India**: patients **swallow the capsule**, breathe out into the device (moisture clumps the powder), inhale too slowly, or store capsules outside the foil - teach that the capsule is only a container. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Multi-dose DPI**: (1) open or uncap; (2) **load with the device held as instructed** (twist the base or slide the lever until it clicks); (3) breathe out away from it; (4) seal lips and breathe in **fast and deep**; (5) hold 5-10 seconds; (6) close it and read the **dose counter** - do not shake or blow into a DPI. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Breath-actuated MDI**: shake, open the cap, breathe out, seal lips and **breathe in slowly and deeply - the dose fires automatically** - then hold 10 seconds; useful when the patient cannot coordinate press and breathe but cannot manage a DPI. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Soft-mist inhaler (tiotropium)**: (1) with the cap closed **turn the base half a turn until it clicks**; (2) open the cap; (3) breathe out; (4) seal lips without covering the air vents; (5) **breathe in slowly and press the button**, continuing to breathe in; (6) hold 10 seconds; (7) repeat for the second puff - the slow mist needs little coordination. [GINA 2025]",
          "**Nebuliser**: fill to **3-4 mL** (drug plus normal saline), mouthpiece in older children and adults and mask in young children, **tidal breathing for 5-10 minutes** until it sputters, oxygen-driven at 6-8 L/min in severe attacks; it is **no better than pMDI with spacer**, costs more and spreads aerosol, so it is not the routine home device. [GINA 2025]",
