      "Community-acquired pneumonia is an **acute lower respiratory infection acquired outside hospital with new radiographic consolidation**; the family physician confirms it with a chest X-ray and pulse oximetry, grades severity with **CURB-65 (CRB-65 in the clinic) plus SpO2**, starts **amoxicillin (plus a macrolide or doxycycline when indicated) within 4 hours for 5 days**, and reviews at 48-72 hours to catch the pneumonia that is really tuberculosis, empyema or cancer.",
