          "**Severe CAP** in hospital is defined by the **IDSA/ATS criteria - 1 major (septic shock on vasopressors or mechanical ventilation) or 3 or more minor** (RR 30 or more, PaO2/FiO2 250 or less, multilobar infiltrates, confusion, BUN 20 mg/dL or more, WBC under 4000, platelets under 1 lakh, temperature under 36 C, hypotension needing aggressive fluids). [IDSA/ATS 2019]",
