          "Organisms reach the alveoli mainly by **microaspiration of colonised oropharyngeal secretions** (during sleep, stroke, alcohol, seizures) and by **inhalation of droplets** (atypicals, influenza, TB); blood-borne seeding (S. aureus from IV drug use) is rare. [Harrison 22e]",
