          "**Exudates** (diseased pleura): in India **tuberculosis** first, then **parapneumonic effusion and empyema**, **malignancy** (lung, breast, lymphoma, ovary, mesothelioma), pulmonary embolism (exudate in about three-quarters), pancreatitis, rheumatoid arthritis, SLE, post-cardiac injury and drugs (methotrexate, amiodarone, nitrofurantoin). [Harrison 22e]",
